{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The equation that results from translating the parabola $y=x^2$ to the right by $\\greenD{h}$ units and up by $\\goldE{k}$ units is:\n\n$y=(x-\\greenD{h})^2+\\goldE{k}$\n\nNote that negative values of $\\greenD{h}$ represent leftward shifts and negative values for $\\goldE{k}$ represent downward shifts.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"To translate the graph of $\\blueD{f}$ to the graph of $\\maroonD{g}$, we shift left $2$ units and up $1$ unit. So $\\greenD{h}=\\greenD{-2}$ and $\\goldE{k}=\\goldE{1}$.\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"Drag the sliders for $h$ and $k$ to see graphs of parabolas.\n\n[[☃ interaction 1]]","hidePrompt":"Hide interaction","showPrompt":"Show me.","static":false,"widgets":{"interaction 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"elements":[{"key":"line-8e8555","options":{"arrows":"","color":"#28AE7B","endX":"-4","endY":"9","startX":"-10","startY":"9","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":2},"type":"line"},{"key":"line-54c1f5","options":{"arrows":"","color":"gray","endX":"-4","endY":"6","startX":"-10","startY":"6","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":2},"type":"line"},{"key":"movable-point-7bc646","options":{"constraint":"none","constraintFn":"0","constraintXMax":"-4","constraintXMin":"-10","constraintYMax":"9","constraintYMin":"9","snap":0.5,"startX":"-7","startY":"9","varSubscript":2},"type":"movable-point"},{"key":"movable-point-877012","options":{"constraint":"none","constraintFn":"0","constraintXMax":"-4","constraintXMin":"-10","constraintYMax":"6","constraintYMin":"6","snap":0.5,"startX":"-7","startY":"6","varSubscript":3},"type":"movable-point"},{"key":"function-25b45e","options":{"color":"#6495ED","funcName":"f","rangeMax":"10","rangeMin":"-10","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":2,"value":"\\left(x-2\\cdot\\left(x_2+7\\right)\\right)^2+2\\cdot\\left(x_3+7\\right)"},"type":"function"},{"key":"label-aaa0ec","options":{"color":"black","coordX":"5","coordY":"7.5","label":"$y=(x-\\greenD h)^2+\\gray k$"},"type":"label"},{"key":"point-89dff","options":{"color":"#6495ED","coordX":"2\\left(x_2+7\\right)","coordY":"2\\left(x_3+7\\right)"},"type":"point"},{"key":"label-a8e7bf","options":{"color":"#28AE7B","coordX":"-3.5","coordY":"9","label":"h"},"type":"label"},{"key":"label-688057","options":{"color":"gray","coordX":"-3.5","coordY":"6","label":"k"},"type":"label"},{"key":"label-33ecb7","options":{"color":"gray","coordX":"-4.5","coordY":"3","label":""},"type":"label"},{"key":"label-12b794","options":{"color":"black","coordX":"-7","coordY":"8","label":"0"},"type":"label"},{"key":"label-abd244","options":{"color":"black","coordX":"-10","coordY":"8","label":"-6"},"type":"label"},{"key":"label-ee5dfa","options":{"color":"black","coordX":"-4","coordY":"8","label":"6"},"type":"label"}],"graph":{"backgroundImage":{"height":0,"url":null,"width":0},"box":[250,250],"editableSettings":["canvas","graph"],"gridStep":[1,1],"labels":["x","y"],"markings":"graph","range":[[-10,10],[-10,10]],"rulerLabel":"","rulerTicks":10,"showProtractor":false,"showRuler":false,"showTooltips":false,"snapStep":[1,1],"tickStep":[2,2],"valid":true},"static":false},"static":false,"type":"interaction","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion:\n\n$g(x)=(x + 2)^2 + 1$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Function $g$ can be thought of as a translated (shifted) version of $f(x)=x^2$.\n\n![A parabola labeled f has a vertex at the point 0, 0. A parabola labeled g has a vertex at the point negative 2,  1.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/6d9bfebb8aa08d341dc0f537da8e39eea295b3d2)\n\n**Write the equation for $g(x)$.**\n\n$g(x)=$ [[☃